# the Mach-O writer, the Mach-O model into bytes
#
# the file is the header and load commands region followed by one region for
# each extent, all placed in order through the layout plan. the commands are
# measured first, the extents are sized, the plan is sealed, the sealed total
# is allocated once and every region is written at the offset the plan
# recorded. every offset and size a load command or section header holds for
# an extent, and every count of a table, is written from the sealed plan, so
# the model never states a number its tables decide. a field with no extent
# keeps the value the model holds. raw pieces are written back byte for byte,
# decoded blobs through the link-edit codecs, and the code signature last:
# its code slots hash the file up to its own offset. an extent the model does
# not hold, a number past the width of its field and a region outside the
# segment that owns it are refused, and nothing is clamped. a load command is
# padded to the width of a pointer. a fat file places each slice at the
# alignment its entry states, with the bytes between slices written as held.

